# MOVED — the environment-variable registry is `.env.example`.
#
# This file briefly claimed to be "the single maintained catalog of every
# configuration value the app reads" (PR #210). That claim was wrong: it was
# missing names the older file had, missing FCI_REHEARSAL_ACKNOWLEDGMENT
# entirely, and pinned by zero tests — while `.env.example` is read and
# enforced by three CI suites (task-tracking-docs, google-chat-secret-leak,
# rendered-html) and is the file AGENTS.md points at.
#
# One registry, one truth: use `.env.example`. Its unique names were merged
# there on July 27, 2026. This stub remains only so the `.dev.vars` local-file
# convention (wrangler reads `.dev.vars`) still has a discoverable anchor:
#
#   copy .env.example -> .dev.vars   and fill in real values there.
#
# LAW (unchanged): real secrets, API keys, tokens, webhook URLs, and client
# secrets are NEVER committed to this repository, pasted into chat/email, or
# shown in the app. The UI reports Configured/Missing by name only.
